WEBVTT

1
00:00:53.637 --> 00:00:55.387
Wow.
Mmm.

2
00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.682
- Wow.
- Mmm-hmm.

3
00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:01.977
- Wow.
- Yes, Marlin.

4
00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:04.104
I see it. It's beautiful.

5
00:01:04.189 --> 00:01:06.899
So, Coral, when you said
you wanted an ocean view,

6
00:01:06.983 --> 00:01:10.694
you didn't think you were going
to get the whole ocean, did you?

7
00:01:12.489 --> 00:01:13.656
Oh, yeah!

8
00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:17.827
A fish can breathe out here. Did
your man deliver or did he deliver?

9
00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:20.329
- My man delivered.
- It wasn't so easy.

10
00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:23.290
A lot of clownfish had
their eyes on this place.

11
00:01:23.375 --> 00:01:27.044
You better believe they did.
Every single one of them.

12
00:01:27.128 --> 00:01:30.381
You did good and the
neighbourhood is awesome.

13
00:01:40.809 --> 00:01:45.855
- So you do like it, don't you?
- No, no, I really do like it.

14
00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:48.899
But, Marlin, I know that
the Drop Off is desirable,

15
00:01:48.984 --> 00:01:50.901
great schools, amazing view,

16
00:01:50.986 --> 00:01:53.529
but do we really
need so much space?

17
00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:56.115
Coral, honey, these are our
kids we're talking about.

18
00:01:56.199 --> 00:01:57.324
They deserve the best.

19
00:01:57.409 --> 00:02:01.704
Look. They'll wake up, poke their
little heads out and see a whale

20
00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:03.914
- right by their bedroom window!
- Shh!

21
00:02:04.374 --> 00:02:07.585
- You're going to wake the kids.
- Oh, right. Right.

22
00:02:11.298 --> 00:02:12.548
Aw, look.

23
00:02:14.009 --> 00:02:15.968
They're dreaming.

24
00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:20.389
- We still have to name them.
- All of them? Right now?

25
00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:23.642
All right. We'll name
this half Marlin Jr.

26
00:02:23.727 --> 00:02:25.853
And this half Coral Jr.

27
00:02:25.937 --> 00:02:28.397
- Okay, we're done.
- I like Nemo.

28
00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:29.899
Nemo?

29
00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:33.777
We'll name one Nemo, but I'd like
most of them to be Marlin Jr.

30
00:02:33.862 --> 00:02:36.780
In a couple of days, we're
going to be parents!

31
00:02:36.865 --> 00:02:37.990
Yeah.

32
00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:41.660
- What if they don't like me?
- Marlin...

33
00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:43.412
There's over 400 eggs.

34
00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:46.665
Odds are one of them
is bound to like you.

35
00:02:50.003 --> 00:02:51.003
What?

36
00:02:51.713 --> 00:02:54.423
- You remember how we met?
- I try not to.

37
00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:55.716
Well, I remember.

38
00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:58.636
Excuse me, Miss. Can you see
if I have a hook in my lip?

39
00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:00.930
- Marlin.
- Look closer.

40
00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:04.224
- Get away!
- Here he is. Cutie's here!

41
00:03:06.603 --> 00:03:08.520
Where did everybody go?

42
00:03:15.445 --> 00:03:17.112
Coral, get inside the house.

43
00:03:19.407 --> 00:03:22.076
No, don't. They'll be fine.
Just get inside.

44
00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:23.827
You. Right now.

45
00:03:26.498 --> 00:03:27.831
No!

46
00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:48.102
Coral!

47
00:03:54.526 --> 00:03:55.526
Coral?

48
00:04:06.287 --> 00:04:07.287
Coral!

49
00:04:17.424 --> 00:04:18.549
Coral?

50
00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:43.699
There, there.

51
00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:45.743
It's okay. Daddy's here.

52
00:04:47.245 --> 00:04:48.954
Daddy's got you.

53
00:04:52.041 --> 00:04:56.211
I promise I will never let
anything happen to you,

54
00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:57.588
Nemo.

55
00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:38.322
First day of school! Wake up!
Come on. First day of school.

56
00:05:39.923 --> 00:05:42.299
I don't want to go to school.

57
00:05:42.383 --> 00:05:44.176
- Not you, Dad. Me.
- Okay.

58
00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:46.261
Get up! Time for school!

59
00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:50.849
- All right, I'm up. It's time for school.
- Oh, boy!

60
00:05:50.934 --> 00:05:52.059
Nemo!

61
00:05:52.143 --> 00:05:54.895
- First day of school!
- Don't move.

62
00:05:54.979 --> 00:05:58.482
You'll never get out of
there yourself. I'll do it.

63
00:05:58.566 --> 00:06:00.400
- You feel a break?
- No.

64
00:06:00.485 --> 00:06:03.654
Sometimes fluid is rushing to
the area. Any rushing fluids?

65
00:06:03.738 --> 00:06:06.448
- No.
- How many stripes do I have?

66
00:06:06.533 --> 00:06:08.450
- Answer the question.
- Three.

67
00:06:08.535 --> 00:06:11.912
No! Something's wrong with you.
I have one, two...

68
00:06:11.996 --> 00:06:13.872
Three. That's all I have?

69
00:06:13.957 --> 00:06:15.958
You're okay. How's
the lucky fin?

70
00:06:16.042 --> 00:06:18.293
- Lucky.
- Let's see.

71
00:06:20.421 --> 00:06:23.215
Sure you want to go
to school this year?

72
00:06:23.299 --> 00:06:27.010
- You can wait five or six years.
- Come on, Dad. It's time for school.

73
00:06:27.679 --> 00:06:29.304
- Forgot to brush.

74
00:06:29.389 --> 00:06:31.849
Do you want this
anemone to sting you?

75
00:06:31.933 --> 00:06:33.392
- Yes.
- Brush.

76
00:06:34.227 --> 00:06:35.978
- I'm done.
- You missed a spot.

77
00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:37.938
- Where?
- There.

78
00:06:38.022 --> 00:06:40.399
Right there. And here and here.

79
00:06:49.659 --> 00:06:54.621
We're excited. First day of school.
Here we go. We're ready to learn.

80
00:06:54.706 --> 00:06:56.915
What do we have to
remember about the ocean?

81
00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:59.501
- It's not safe.
- That's my boy.

82
00:06:59.586 --> 00:07:04.381
First, we check to see that the coast
is clear. We go out and back in.

83
00:07:04.465 --> 00:07:06.675
Then we go out and back in.

84
00:07:06.759 --> 00:07:09.678
Then one more time.
Out and back in.

85
00:07:09.762 --> 00:07:12.431
- If you want to do it four times...
- Dad...

86
00:07:12.515 --> 00:07:14.433
All right. Come on, boy.

87
00:07:16.936 --> 00:07:19.771
Maybe while I'm at school,
I'll see a shark.

88
00:07:19.856 --> 00:07:22.482
- I doubt that.
- Have you ever met a shark?

89
00:07:22.567 --> 00:07:25.235
- No, and I don't plan to.
- How old are sea turtles?

90
00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:27.529
Sea turtles? I don't know.

91
00:07:27.614 --> 00:07:30.032
Sandy Plankton from
next door said that

92
00:07:30.116 --> 00:07:34.286
sea turtles live to be
about 100 years old.

93
00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:38.916
If I ever meet a sea turtle, I'll ask
him, after I'm done talking to the shark.

94
00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:41.043
Hold on. Wait to cross.

95
00:07:42.503 --> 00:07:44.671
Hold my fin. Hold my fin.

96
00:07:44.756 --> 00:07:48.008
You're not going to freak out
like you did at the petting zoo.

97
00:07:48.092 --> 00:07:50.636
That snail was about to charge.

98
00:07:51.429 --> 00:07:53.555
I wonder where we're
supposed to go.

99
00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:56.767
- Bye, Mom.
- I'll pick you up after school.

100
00:07:58.645 --> 00:08:01.563
Come on, you guys. Stop it.
Give it back.

101
00:08:02.649 --> 00:08:04.650
Come on. We'll try over there.

102
00:08:05.818 --> 00:08:08.654
Excuse me. Is this where
we meet his teacher?

103
00:08:08.738 --> 00:08:12.240
- Look who's out of the anemone.
- Yes, shocking, I know.

104
00:08:12.325 --> 00:08:13.700
- Marty?
- Marlin.

105
00:08:13.785 --> 00:08:14.785
- Bob.
- Ted.

106
00:08:14.827 --> 00:08:16.828
Phil. Hey, you're a clownfish.

107
00:08:17.497 --> 00:08:19.706
You're funny, right?
Tell us a joke.

108
00:08:19.791 --> 00:08:22.084
- Yeah.
- Good idea.

109
00:08:22.168 --> 00:08:26.380
That's a misconception. Clownfish
are no funnier than any other fish.

110
00:08:26.464 --> 00:08:28.924
- Come on, Clowny.
- Do something funny.

111
00:08:29.008 --> 00:08:31.259
All right. I know one joke.

112
00:08:32.470 --> 00:08:35.389
There's a mollusk.
He walks up to...

113
00:08:35.473 --> 00:08:37.182
Well, he swims up.

114
00:08:37.350 --> 00:08:41.103
Actually, the mollusk isn't
moving. He's in one place.

115
00:08:41.187 --> 00:08:42.604
And then the sea cucumber...

116
00:08:43.523 --> 00:08:46.900
I'm mixed up. There was a
mollusk and a sea cucumber.

117
00:08:46.985 --> 00:08:48.819
None of them were walking...

118
00:08:48.903 --> 00:08:52.030
Sheldon! Get out of
Mr. Johanssen's yard now!

119
00:08:52.949 --> 00:08:55.117
All right, you kids!

120
00:08:55.201 --> 00:08:57.244
Where'd you go? Where'd you go?

121
00:08:57.328 --> 00:08:59.705
Can I go play, too? Can I?

122
00:08:59.789 --> 00:09:02.541
I would feel better if you go
play over on the sponge beds.

123
00:09:07.839 --> 00:09:09.006
That's where I would play.

124
00:09:10.842 --> 00:09:14.094
- What's wrong with his fin?
- He looks funny.

125
00:09:14.178 --> 00:09:17.639
- Hey, what did I do? - Be nice.
- It's his first time at school.

126
00:09:17.724 --> 00:09:20.225
He was born with it. We
call it his lucky fin.

127
00:09:20.309 --> 00:09:21.351
Dad...

128
00:09:21.436 --> 00:09:25.188
See this tentacle? It's shorter
than all my other tentacles.

129
00:09:25.273 --> 00:09:29.651
But you can't really tell. Especially
when I twirl them like this.

130
00:09:29.736 --> 00:09:31.737
I'm H20 intolerant.

131
00:09:32.697 --> 00:09:34.239
I'm obnoxious.

132
00:09:35.283 --> 00:09:38.243
Let's name the zones,
the zones, the zones

133
00:09:38.327 --> 00:09:41.038
Let's name the zones
of the open sea

134
00:09:41.122 --> 00:09:42.456
Mr. Ray!

135
00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:44.583
- Come on, Nemo.
- Stay with me.

136
00:09:44.667 --> 00:09:47.502
There's epipelagic, mesopelagic,
bathyal, abyssopelagic

137
00:09:47.587 --> 00:09:51.089
All the rest are too
deep for you and me to see

138
00:09:51.174 --> 00:09:53.842
I wonder where my
class has gone.

139
00:09:53.926 --> 00:09:55.719
We're under here.

140
00:09:55.803 --> 00:09:59.514
There you are! Come
aboard, explorers.

141
00:09:59.599 --> 00:10:02.142
Knowledge exploring
is oh so lyrical

142
00:10:02.226 --> 00:10:04.686
When you think thoughts
that are empirical

143
00:10:04.771 --> 00:10:06.021
Dad, you can go now.

144
00:10:06.105 --> 00:10:09.066
- Well, hello. Who is this?
- I'm Nemo.

145
00:10:09.150 --> 00:10:12.694
Nemo, all new explorers must
answer a science question.

146
00:10:12.779 --> 00:10:15.697
- Okay.
- You live in what kind of home?

147
00:10:15.782 --> 00:10:19.951
In an anemoninny.
Anemonemenemone.

148
00:10:20.036 --> 00:10:22.412
Don't hurt yourself.
Welcome aboard.

149
00:10:22.497 --> 00:10:24.539
Just so you know, he's
got a little fin.

150
00:10:24.624 --> 00:10:28.126
If he's having trouble swimming,
let him take a break. 15 minutes.

151
00:10:28.211 --> 00:10:30.378
Dad, it's time for
you to go now.

152
00:10:30.463 --> 00:10:32.547
We're going to stay together.

153
00:10:32.632 --> 00:10:35.258
Okay, class. Optical
orbits up front.

154
00:10:35.343 --> 00:10:39.721
Remember, we keep our supraesophageal
ganglion to ourselves.

155
00:10:39.806 --> 00:10:42.516
- That means you, Jimmy.
- Oh, man!

156
00:10:43.768 --> 00:10:45.977
- Bye, Nemo.
- Bye, Dad.

157
00:10:46.646 --> 00:10:47.729
Bye, son.

158
00:10:50.441 --> 00:10:52.067
Be safe.

159
00:10:52.151 --> 00:10:54.569
You're doing well
for a first-timer.

160
00:10:54.654 --> 00:10:56.905
You can't hold on to
them forever, can you?

161
00:10:56.989 --> 00:11:00.200
I had a tough time when my
eldest went out on the Drop Off.

162
00:11:00.284 --> 00:11:02.828
The Drop Off! They're
going to the Drop Off?

163
00:11:02.912 --> 00:11:04.538
Are you insane?

164
00:11:04.622 --> 00:11:07.499
Why don't we fry them up now
and serve them with chips?

165
00:11:07.583 --> 00:11:09.209
Hey, Marty, calm down.

166
00:11:09.293 --> 00:11:11.086
Don't tell me to
be calm, pony-boy.

167
00:11:12.171 --> 00:11:13.839
Pony-boy?

168
00:11:13.923 --> 00:11:16.550
For a clownfish, he
really isn't that funny.

169
00:11:16.634 --> 00:11:17.634
Pity.

170
00:11:20.138 --> 00:11:22.264
Let's name the species,
the species, the species

171
00:11:22.348 --> 00:11:25.183
Let's name the species
that live in the sea

172
00:11:31.107 --> 00:11:33.942
Mollusca and gastropoda,
arthropoda, echinoderma, chordata

173
00:11:34.026 --> 00:11:35.306
And some fish
like you and me!

174
00:11:35.361 --> 00:11:37.279
Come on. Sing with me.

175
00:11:46.539 --> 00:11:48.957
Seaweed is cool,
seaweed is fun

176
00:11:49.041 --> 00:11:51.042
It makes its food from
the rays of the sun

177
00:11:53.754 --> 00:11:55.839
Okay, the Drop Off.

178
00:11:55.923 --> 00:11:59.217
All right, kids. Feel free
to explore, but stay close.

179
00:11:59.719 --> 00:12:01.970
Stromatolitic cyanobacteria!
Gather.

180
00:12:02.054 --> 00:12:05.265
An ecosystem contained in
one infinitesimal speck.

181
00:12:07.518 --> 00:12:09.394
Come on. Let's go.

182
00:12:10.062 --> 00:12:11.354
Come on. Sing with me.

183
00:12:11.439 --> 00:12:14.441
There's porifera, coelenterata,
hydrozoa, scyphozoa

184
00:12:14.525 --> 00:12:16.086
Anthozoa, ctenophora,
bryozoas three

185
00:12:16.944 --> 00:12:18.862
Hey, guys, wait up.

186
00:12:19.864 --> 00:12:21.239
Whoa!

187
00:12:24.827 --> 00:12:26.411
Cool.

188
00:12:28.581 --> 00:12:30.207
Saved your life!

189
00:12:30.917 --> 00:12:33.710
- You guys made me ink.

190
00:12:33.794 --> 00:12:35.003
What's that?

191
00:12:36.839 --> 00:12:39.424
I know what that is.
Sandy Plankton saw one.

192
00:12:40.384 --> 00:12:42.636
He said it was called a butt.

193
00:12:43.596 --> 00:12:46.389
Wow. That's a pretty big butt.

194
00:12:48.017 --> 00:12:51.436
Look at me. I'm going
to go touch the butt.

195
00:12:54.106 --> 00:12:56.399
Oh, yeah? Let's see
you get closer.

196
00:12:56.484 --> 00:12:57.776
Okay.

197
00:12:59.237 --> 00:13:00.612
Beat that.

198
00:13:01.155 --> 00:13:03.198
Come on, Nemo. How
far can you go?

199
00:13:04.450 --> 00:13:07.577
- My dad says it's not safe.
- Nemo, no!

200
00:13:07.662 --> 00:13:08.787
Dad?

201
00:13:08.871 --> 00:13:10.497
You were about to
swim into open water.

202
00:13:10.581 --> 00:13:11.581
No!

203
00:13:11.666 --> 00:13:13.458
Good thing I was here.

204
00:13:13.542 --> 00:13:15.961
- He wasn't going to go.
- He was too afraid.

205
00:13:16.045 --> 00:13:18.588
- I wasn't.
- This does not concern you.

206
00:13:18.673 --> 00:13:22.133
You're lucky I don't tell your
parents. You can't swim well.

207
00:13:22.218 --> 00:13:25.428
- I can swim fine, Dad, okay?
- No. It's not okay.

208
00:13:25.513 --> 00:13:26.972
You shouldn't be near here.

209
00:13:27.306 --> 00:13:29.641
You'll start school
in a year or two.

210
00:13:29.725 --> 00:13:32.811
No. Just because you're
scared of the ocean...

211
00:13:32.895 --> 00:13:34.813
Clearly you're not ready.

212
00:13:34.897 --> 00:13:37.857
You think you can do these
things, but you just can't!

213
00:13:39.443 --> 00:13:40.819
I hate you.

214
00:13:42.321 --> 00:13:45.031
There's...

215
00:13:45.116 --> 00:13:46.908
Nothing to see. Gather there.

216
00:13:46.993 --> 00:13:50.287
Anything I can do? I am a
scientist. Is there any problem?

217
00:13:50.371 --> 00:13:53.540
I didn't mean to interrupt.
He isn't a good swimmer.

218
00:13:53.624 --> 00:13:56.793
I think it's too soon for him
to be out here unsupervised.

219
00:13:56.877 --> 00:13:59.087
I can assure you,
he's quite safe with me.

220
00:13:59.171 --> 00:14:00.338
I'm sure he is.

221
00:14:00.631 --> 00:14:03.675
But you have a large class and
he can get lost from sight

222
00:14:03.801 --> 00:14:05.635
if you're not looking.

223
00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:08.513
Oh, my gosh! Nemo's
swimming out to sea.

224
00:14:10.516 --> 00:14:11.683
Nemo!

225
00:14:13.227 --> 00:14:14.769
What do you think you're doing?

226
00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:17.814
You're going to get stuck

227
00:14:17.898 --> 00:14:20.775
and I'm going to have to get
you before another fish does.

228
00:14:21.652 --> 00:14:23.486
Get back here.

229
00:14:23.571 --> 00:14:26.031
I said get back here now!

230
00:14:27.241 --> 00:14:28.825
Stop.

231
00:14:28.909 --> 00:14:30.952
You take one more
move, mister...

232
00:14:32.079 --> 00:14:35.332
Don't you dare. If you put
one fin on that boat...

233
00:14:35.416 --> 00:14:36.916
Are you listening to me?

234
00:14:37.001 --> 00:14:39.044
Don't touch the boa...

235
00:14:39.128 --> 00:14:40.128
Nemo!

236
00:14:40.421 --> 00:14:41.796
He touched the butt.

237
00:14:41.881 --> 00:14:44.674
You paddle your little
tail back here.

238
00:14:44.759 --> 00:14:47.552
That's right. You are in
big trouble, young man.

239
00:14:47.636 --> 00:14:49.721
Do you hear me? Big...

240
00:14:55.311 --> 00:14:56.311
Aagghh!

241
00:14:56.395 --> 00:14:58.480
Daddy, help me!

242
00:14:59.148 --> 00:15:01.066
I'm coming, Nemo.

243
00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:04.652
Get under me, kids.

244
00:15:05.738 --> 00:15:07.405
No! Dad!

245
00:15:15.331 --> 00:15:16.414
Nemo!

246
00:15:20.252 --> 00:15:22.337
Nemo! Nemo, no!

247
00:15:23.589 --> 00:15:24.714
Nemo!

248
00:15:24.799 --> 00:15:26.007
Nemo, Nemo!

249
00:15:26.467 --> 00:15:27.467
No!

250
00:15:41.190 --> 00:15:42.941
Nemo, Nemo!

251
00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:54.494
Hold on!

252
00:16:06.924 --> 00:16:07.966
Oh, no.

253
00:16:08.426 --> 00:16:10.552
No. It's gone. It's gone.

254
00:16:10.636 --> 00:16:12.971
It can't be gone. No. No!

255
00:16:13.055 --> 00:16:15.223
Nemo! Nemo...

256
00:16:15.808 --> 00:16:17.517
Nemo!

257
00:16:17.601 --> 00:16:18.810
No.

258
00:16:20.438 --> 00:16:22.564
Nemo! Nemo!

259
00:16:22.648 --> 00:16:23.690
No.

260
00:16:23.774 --> 00:16:25.233
No. Please, no.

261
00:16:28.070 --> 00:16:29.154
No, no.

262
00:16:31.824 --> 00:16:33.408
Has anybody seen a boat?

263
00:16:33.492 --> 00:16:35.326
Please. A white boat?

264
00:16:35.411 --> 00:16:37.829
My son! My son!

265
00:16:37.913 --> 00:16:39.247
Help me. Please.

266
00:16:39.331 --> 00:16:40.665
Look out!

267
00:16:45.463 --> 00:16:48.089
Oh, sorry. I didn't
see you, Sir.

268
00:16:48.174 --> 00:16:49.591
Are you okay?

269
00:16:49.675 --> 00:16:51.342
- He's gone.
- There, there.

270
00:16:51.427 --> 00:16:53.094
- He's gone.
- It's all right.

271
00:16:53.179 --> 00:16:55.597
- It'll be okay.
- No, they took him away.

272
00:16:55.681 --> 00:16:57.265
I have to find the boat.

273
00:16:57.349 --> 00:16:59.934
- A boat? I've seen a boat.
- You have?

274
00:17:00.019 --> 00:17:03.062
- And it passed by not too long ago.
- A white one?

275
00:17:03.147 --> 00:17:05.273
- Hi. I'm Dory.
- Where? Which way?

276
00:17:05.357 --> 00:17:08.276
Oh. It went this way.

277
00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:10.612
- Follow me.
- Thank you.

278
00:17:10.696 --> 00:17:12.071
Thank you so much.

279
00:17:12.156 --> 00:17:13.656
No problem.

280
00:17:40.226 --> 00:17:41.309
Wait.

281
00:17:48.317 --> 00:17:52.362
Quit it. I'm trying to swim here.
The ocean isn't big enough for you?

282
00:17:52.446 --> 00:17:54.572
You got a problem, buddy?

283
00:17:54.657 --> 00:17:55.907
Do you? Do you?

284
00:17:55.991 --> 00:17:58.117
Want a piece of me? Yeah.

285
00:17:58.202 --> 00:17:59.744
I'm scared now!

286
00:17:59.828 --> 00:18:01.829
- Wait.
- Stop following me, okay?

287
00:18:01.914 --> 00:18:04.999
What? You're showing me
which way the boat went.

288
00:18:05.084 --> 00:18:08.753
A boat? I've seen a boat. It
passed by not too long ago.

289
00:18:08.837 --> 00:18:11.756
It went this way. Follow me.

290
00:18:11.840 --> 00:18:13.841
Wait a minute. What is going on?

291
00:18:13.926 --> 00:18:15.969
You already told me which
way the boat was going.

292
00:18:16.637 --> 00:18:19.222
I did? Oh, no.

293
00:18:19.306 --> 00:18:23.101
If this is some kind of joke,
it's not funny and I know funny.

294
00:18:23.185 --> 00:18:27.397
- I'm a clownfish.
- No, it's not. I'm so sorry.

295
00:18:27.898 --> 00:18:30.858
See, I suffer from
short-term memory loss.

296
00:18:30.943 --> 00:18:33.278
Short-term memory loss.

297
00:18:33.362 --> 00:18:35.196
- I don't believe this.
- No.

298
00:18:35.281 --> 00:18:38.783
I forget things almost
instantly. It runs in my family.

299
00:18:38.867 --> 00:18:42.120
At least I think it does.
Uh... Hmm.

300
00:18:42.955 --> 00:18:44.455
Where are they?

301
00:18:49.086 --> 00:18:50.211
Can I help you?

302
00:18:51.130 --> 00:18:53.506
Something's wrong with you.
Really.

303
00:18:53.591 --> 00:18:55.383
You're wasting my time.

304
00:18:55.467 --> 00:18:57.343
I have to find my son.

305
00:19:00.723 --> 00:19:01.806
Hello.

306
00:19:02.641 --> 00:19:03.933
Well, hi!

307
00:19:04.893 --> 00:19:06.436
Name's Bruce.

308
00:19:07.146 --> 00:19:09.188
It's all right. I understand.

309
00:19:09.273 --> 00:19:11.691
Why trust a shark, right?

310
00:19:19.867 --> 00:19:24.412
So, what's a couple of bites
like you doing out so late?

311
00:19:24.496 --> 00:19:26.456
Nothing. We're not even out.

312
00:19:26.540 --> 00:19:27.790
Great.

313
00:19:27.875 --> 00:19:32.378
Then how would you morsels like to come
to a little get-together I'm having?

314
00:19:32.463 --> 00:19:36.674
- You mean like a party?
- Yeah, right. A party.

315
00:19:36.759 --> 00:19:39.927
- What do you say? - I love
parties. That sounds like fun.

316
00:19:40.012 --> 00:19:43.598
Parties are fun and it's tempting,
but we can't because...

317
00:19:43.682 --> 00:19:46.100
Come on. I insist.

318
00:19:46.185 --> 00:19:48.686
Okay. That's all that matters.

319
00:19:52.149 --> 00:19:54.484
Look. Balloons.
It is a party.

320
00:19:55.361 --> 00:19:59.489
Mind your distance, though. Those
balloons can be a bit dodgy.

321
00:19:59.573 --> 00:20:01.324
You wouldn't want
one of them to pop.

322
00:20:16.507 --> 00:20:17.965
Anchor! Chum!

323
00:20:19.051 --> 00:20:20.802
There you are, Bruce. Finally.

324
00:20:20.886 --> 00:20:23.680
- We got company.
- It's about time, mate.

325
00:20:23.764 --> 00:20:26.641
We've gone through the
snacks and I'm starving.

326
00:20:26.725 --> 00:20:28.851
We almost had to have
a feeding frenzy.

327
00:20:28.936 --> 00:20:30.561
Let's get this over with.

328
00:20:32.856 --> 00:20:36.150
Right then. The meeting has
officially come to order.

329
00:20:36.235 --> 00:20:37.860
Let us all say the pledge.

330
00:20:37.945 --> 00:20:39.821
I am a nice shark,

331
00:20:39.905 --> 00:20:42.281
not a mindless eating machine.

332
00:20:42.366 --> 00:20:47.036
If I am to change this image,
I must first change myself.

333
00:20:47.246 --> 00:20:49.789
Fish are friends, not food.

334
00:20:49.873 --> 00:20:51.499
Except stinking dolphins.

335
00:20:51.583 --> 00:20:54.460
Dolphins! Yeah, they
think they're so cute.

336
00:20:54.545 --> 00:20:58.673
Look, I'm a flipping little dolphin. Let
me flip for you. Ain't I something?

337
00:20:58.757 --> 00:21:02.301
Today's meeting is step
five Bring a Fish Friend.

338
00:21:02.386 --> 00:21:04.595
- Do you all have your friends?
- Got mine.

339
00:21:06.932 --> 00:21:09.100
Hey there! How about you, Chum?

340
00:21:09.184 --> 00:21:12.895
Well, I seem to
have misplaced my

341
00:21:12.980 --> 00:21:14.605
friend.

342
00:21:15.441 --> 00:21:16.649
It's all right, Chum.

343
00:21:16.734 --> 00:21:19.652
Help yourself to
one of my friends.

344
00:21:19.737 --> 00:21:23.197
Thanks, mate. A
little chum for Chum.

345
00:21:23.282 --> 00:21:26.909
I'll start the testimonies.
Hello. My name is Bruce.

346
00:21:26.994 --> 00:21:28.202
Hello, Bruce.

347
00:21:28.287 --> 00:21:31.497
It has been three weeks since
my last fish, on my honour,

348
00:21:31.582 --> 00:21:33.875
or may I be chopped up
and made into soup.

349
00:21:34.585 --> 00:21:36.753
- You're an inspiration to us.
- Amen.

350
00:21:38.005 --> 00:21:40.715
- Right, then. Who's next?
- Pick me. Pick me.

351
00:21:40.799 --> 00:21:42.633
- The little Sheila down the front.
- Whoo!

352
00:21:43.385 --> 00:21:44.969
Come on up here.

353
00:21:46.221 --> 00:21:47.638
Hi. I'm Dory.

354
00:21:47.723 --> 00:21:49.265
Hello, Dory.

355
00:21:49.349 --> 00:21:52.685
And... Well, I don't think
I've ever eaten a fish.

356
00:21:54.146 --> 00:21:56.814
- Hey, that's incredible.
- Good on you, mate!

357
00:21:57.441 --> 00:21:58.900
I'm glad I got
that off my chest.

358
00:21:58.984 --> 00:22:03.196
Anyone else? How about you,
mate? What's your problem?

359
00:22:03.280 --> 00:22:05.615
Me? I don't have a problem.

360
00:22:06.116 --> 00:22:08.159
- Okay.
- Denial.

361
00:22:08.577 --> 00:22:10.536
Just start with your name.

362
00:22:10.621 --> 00:22:12.872
Okay. Hello.

363
00:22:13.248 --> 00:22:16.000
My name is Marlin.
I'm a clownfish.

364
00:22:16.084 --> 00:22:19.587
- A clownfish? Really?
- Go on. Tell us a joke.

365
00:22:19.671 --> 00:22:20.838
I love jokes.

366
00:22:21.131 --> 00:22:24.133
I actually do know one
that's pretty good.

367
00:22:25.177 --> 00:22:28.638
There was this mollusk and he
walks up to a sea cucumber.

368
00:22:28.722 --> 00:22:32.141
Normally they don't talk, but
in a joke, everyone talks.

369
00:22:32.226 --> 00:22:35.228
The sea mollusk says
to the cucumber...

370
00:22:37.773 --> 00:22:39.023
Daddy!

371
00:22:39.566 --> 00:22:40.650
Nemo!

372
00:22:41.026 --> 00:22:42.860
Nemo!

373
00:22:43.612 --> 00:22:45.947
- I don't get it. - For a
clownfish he's not that funny.

374
00:22:46.031 --> 00:22:50.493
No, he's my son. He was
taken by these divers.

375
00:22:51.161 --> 00:22:53.037
You poor fish.

376
00:22:53.121 --> 00:22:56.415
- Humans. Think they own everything.
- Probably American.

377
00:22:56.500 --> 00:23:00.545
There is a father
looking for his little boy.

378
00:23:01.004 --> 00:23:02.672
What do these
markings mean?

379
00:23:02.756 --> 00:23:06.634
- I never knew my father.
- Come here.

380
00:23:06.718 --> 00:23:08.845
- We're all mates here.
- I can't read human.

381
00:23:08.929 --> 00:23:12.014
Then we've got to find a fish
that can read this. Look. Sharks!

382
00:23:12.558 --> 00:23:14.433
- Guys.
- No, Dory.

383
00:23:14.518 --> 00:23:16.894
- That's mine. Give it back.
- Cut it out.

384
00:23:17.062 --> 00:23:20.648
- Ow!
- I'm sorry. Are you okay?

385
00:23:20.732 --> 00:23:23.568
You really clocked me there.
Am I bleeding?

386
00:23:25.070 --> 00:23:27.572
Dory, are you oka...

387
00:23:27.656 --> 00:23:29.156
Oh!

388
00:23:30.242 --> 00:23:31.742
That's good.

389
00:23:32.244 --> 00:23:33.619
Intervention!

390
00:23:34.371 --> 00:23:37.331
- Just a bite.
- You hold it together, mate.

391
00:23:37.416 --> 00:23:40.251
- Fish are friends, not food.
- Food!

392
00:23:41.086 --> 00:23:42.837
Dory, look out.

393
00:23:42.921 --> 00:23:45.798
I'm having fish tonight.

394
00:23:45.883 --> 00:23:47.174
Remember the steps, mate.

395
00:23:53.015 --> 00:23:54.223
Just one bite.

396
00:23:58.770 --> 00:23:59.812
G'day.

397
00:24:03.609 --> 00:24:06.110
There's no way out. There's
got to be a way to escape.

398
00:24:08.739 --> 00:24:11.073
- Who is it?
- Help me find a way out.

399
00:24:11.158 --> 00:24:13.951
Sorry. You'll have to come back
later. We're trying to escape.

400
00:24:14.870 --> 00:24:17.455
There's no way out. There's
got to be a way out.

401
00:24:17.539 --> 00:24:21.709
Here's something. "Es-ca-pé."
I wonder what that means.

402
00:24:21.793 --> 00:24:23.954
- It's spelled just like the
word "escape." - Let's go.

403
00:24:24.463 --> 00:24:27.048
Here's Brucie!

404
00:24:27.549 --> 00:24:31.177
- Wait a minute. You can read?
- I can read? That's right!

405
00:24:31.261 --> 00:24:32.762
Then here. Read this now.

406
00:24:34.806 --> 00:24:37.767
He doesn't mean it. He never
even knew his father.

407
00:24:37.851 --> 00:24:39.894
Don't fall off the wagon.

408
00:24:43.649 --> 00:24:45.441
Oh, no! It's blocked.

409
00:24:49.863 --> 00:24:51.113
No, Bruce!

410
00:24:51.448 --> 00:24:53.658
Sorry about... Bruce, mate.

411
00:24:53.742 --> 00:24:55.910
He's really... A nice guy.

412
00:24:55.994 --> 00:24:57.578
I need to get that mask.

413
00:24:57.663 --> 00:24:59.121
You want that mask? Okay.

414
00:24:59.206 --> 00:25:01.582
No, no, no, no!

415
00:25:02.584 --> 00:25:04.210
Quick. Grab the mask.

416
00:25:08.966 --> 00:25:11.258
Oh, no. Bruce.

417
00:25:11.343 --> 00:25:12.510
What?

418
00:25:14.680 --> 00:25:17.431
Swim away!

419
00:25:17.516 --> 00:25:18.933
Is the party over?

420
00:25:28.819 --> 00:25:30.111
Nice.

421
00:25:33.782 --> 00:25:35.074
Dad!

422
00:25:37.744 --> 00:25:39.120
Daddy?

423
00:26:02.144 --> 00:26:03.310
Barbara.

424
00:26:03.395 --> 00:26:05.236
Prep for his anterior
crown, would you, please?

425
00:26:05.564 --> 00:26:08.691
- And I'll need more cotton rolls.
- All right.

426
00:26:11.737 --> 00:26:12.820
Hello, little fella.

427
00:26:14.239 --> 00:26:15.239
Beauty, isn't he?

428
00:26:15.323 --> 00:26:18.826
I found that guy struggling
for life and I saved him.

429
00:26:18.910 --> 00:26:21.454
- Has that Novocain kicked in yet?

430
00:26:25.208 --> 00:26:26.459
Bubbles!

431
00:26:30.047 --> 00:26:32.965
- My bubbles.
- He likes bubbles.

432
00:26:44.311 --> 00:26:45.436
- Bonjour.
- Aagghh!

433
00:26:46.354 --> 00:26:50.024
Slow down, little fella. There's
nothing to worry about.

434
00:26:50.108 --> 00:26:52.318
- He's scared to death.
- I want to go home.

435
00:26:53.236 --> 00:26:54.653
Do you know where my dad is?

436
00:26:54.738 --> 00:26:57.364
Your dad's probably
back at the pet store.

437
00:26:57.449 --> 00:26:58.783
Pet store?

438
00:26:58.867 --> 00:27:01.994
- Like I'm from Bob's Fish Mart.
- Pet Palace.

439
00:27:02.079 --> 00:27:03.496
- Fish-O-Rama.
- Mail order.

440
00:27:03.580 --> 00:27:04.830
EBay.

441
00:27:04.915 --> 00:27:07.374
- Which one is it?
- I'm from the ocean.

442
00:27:07.459 --> 00:27:10.753
Ah, the ocean. The ocean!
Aagghh!

443
00:27:11.171 --> 00:27:14.090
He hasn't been
decontaminated yet. Jacques!

444
00:27:14.174 --> 00:27:15.508
- Clean him!
- Oui.

445
00:27:17.094 --> 00:27:18.636
- Ocean.
- La mer.

446
00:27:21.473 --> 00:27:22.973
Voilà. He is clean.

447
00:27:25.977 --> 00:27:29.105
Wow. The big blue.
What's it like?

448
00:27:29.648 --> 00:27:31.941
Uh... Big and blue?

449
00:27:32.025 --> 00:27:33.067
I knew it.

450
00:27:33.151 --> 00:27:36.570
If there's anything you need,
ask your Auntie Deb. That's me.

451
00:27:36.655 --> 00:27:41.242
If I'm not around you can always talk
to my sister, Flo. Hi. How are you?

452
00:27:41.326 --> 00:27:44.411
Don't listen to anything my
sister says. She's nuts.

453
00:27:45.664 --> 00:27:48.624
- Can't hear you, Peach.
- I said we got a live one.

454
00:27:48.708 --> 00:27:50.084
- Yes!
- Boy, oh, boy.

455
00:27:50.168 --> 00:27:52.336
- What have we got?
- Root canal.

456
00:27:52.420 --> 00:27:53.671
It's not going to be pretty.

457
00:27:54.422 --> 00:27:55.422
Aagghh!

458
00:27:55.507 --> 00:27:56.924
- Clamp installed?
- Yup.

459
00:27:57.008 --> 00:28:00.427
- What did he use to open? - Glidden
drill. He favours that one.

460
00:28:01.263 --> 00:28:03.430
I can't see, Flo.

461
00:28:04.182 --> 00:28:05.599
Agh!

462
00:28:05.684 --> 00:28:08.269
- Schilder Technique.
- That's a Hedstrom file.

463
00:28:08.353 --> 00:28:10.813
That's not a Hedstrom file.
That's a K-Flex.

464
00:28:10.897 --> 00:28:13.899
It's got a teardrop cross
section. A Hedstrom.

465
00:28:13.984 --> 00:28:16.652
- K-Flex!
- Hedstrom!

466
00:28:16.736 --> 00:28:18.821
There I go. Little help.
Over here.

467
00:28:18.905 --> 00:28:20.781
I'll go deflate him.

468
00:28:20.991 --> 00:28:21.991
Pffft!

469
00:28:22.742 --> 00:28:24.994
All right. Go ahead and rinse.

470
00:28:25.954 --> 00:28:28.372
The human mouth is a
disgusting place.

471
00:28:31.209 --> 00:28:32.835
- Nigel.
- What did I Miss?

472
00:28:32.919 --> 00:28:35.921
- Root canal. A doozy.
- What did he use to open?

473
00:28:36.006 --> 00:28:37.673
- Glidden drill.
- He favours it.

474
00:28:37.757 --> 00:28:40.926
Hope he doesn't get surplus
sealer at the portal terminus.

475
00:28:41.011 --> 00:28:43.971
- Hello. Who's this?
- New guy.

476
00:28:44.055 --> 00:28:46.640
- The dentist took him off the reef.
- An outie.

477
00:28:46.725 --> 00:28:49.476
From my neck of the woods?
Sorry if I took a snap at you.

478
00:28:49.561 --> 00:28:51.812
Fish got to swim.
Birds got to eat.

479
00:28:51.897 --> 00:28:56.275
No, no. Those aren't your fish.
They're my fish. Come on. Go. Shoo.

480
00:28:59.029 --> 00:29:02.281
The picture broke. This
here's Darla. She's my niece.

481
00:29:02.365 --> 00:29:03.486
Going to be eight this week.

482
00:29:03.491 --> 00:29:06.660
Hey, little fella. Say
hello to your new mummy.

483
00:29:06.745 --> 00:29:09.163
She's going to be here
Friday to pick you up.

484
00:29:09.247 --> 00:29:11.040
You're her present.

485
00:29:11.166 --> 00:29:13.125
Shh! It's our little secret.

486
00:29:13.210 --> 00:29:14.501
Well, Mr. Tucker,

487
00:29:14.586 --> 00:29:17.922
while that sets up, I'm going to
go see a man about a wallaby.

488
00:29:19.549 --> 00:29:20.674
Uh-oh. Darla!

489
00:29:20.759 --> 00:29:24.428
- What's wrong with her? - She
wouldn't stop shaking the bag.

490
00:29:25.722 --> 00:29:28.974
- Poor Chuckles.
- He was her present last year.

491
00:29:29.059 --> 00:29:31.769
Hitched a ride on the
porcelain express.

492
00:29:33.438 --> 00:29:35.314
She's a fish killer.

493
00:29:36.274 --> 00:29:39.902
I can't go with that girl. I
have to get back to my dad.

494
00:29:41.029 --> 00:29:44.281
- Daddy! Help me!
- He's stuck.

495
00:29:49.537 --> 00:29:51.288
Nobody touch him.

496
00:29:57.254 --> 00:29:58.545
Can you help me?

497
00:29:58.630 --> 00:30:01.966
No. You got yourself in there,
you can get yourself out.

498
00:30:02.050 --> 00:30:04.802
- Gill... - I just want
to see him do it, okay?

499
00:30:04.886 --> 00:30:08.389
Calm down. Alternate wiggling
your fins and your tail.

500
00:30:08.473 --> 00:30:11.392
I can't. I have a bad fin.

501
00:30:11.476 --> 00:30:13.185
Never stopped me.

502
00:30:17.565 --> 00:30:19.817
Just think about
what you need to do.

503
00:30:24.239 --> 00:30:25.406
Come on.

504
00:30:29.744 --> 00:30:30.744
Perfect.

505
00:30:30.829 --> 00:30:33.664
- You did it.
- Good squirming.

506
00:30:34.833 --> 00:30:37.960
Wow, from the ocean!
Just like you, Gill.

507
00:30:38.044 --> 00:30:39.253
Yeah.

508
00:30:40.088 --> 00:30:43.299
I've seen that look before.
What are you thinking about?

509
00:30:43.383 --> 00:30:48.345
I'm thinking tonight we give
the kid a proper reception.

510
00:30:48.847 --> 00:30:51.724
- So, kid, you got a name or what?
- Nemo.

511
00:30:51.808 --> 00:30:53.225
I'm Nemo.

512
00:30:54.394 --> 00:30:58.147
Nemo.

513
00:31:02.861 --> 00:31:04.862
You going to eat that?
